.TH HD-BACKUP 1 "October 2026" "hd-backup" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-backup \- back up filesets to hard drives and tape
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-backup
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-backup
writes backups of filesets as tarballs in pax format, to mounted hard drives
or to LTO tape.
It keeps track of every file it protects in a SQLite database: the first write
of a backup is a full backup, every following write only holds what is not on
the backup yet.
When a carrier, a drive or a tape, runs full, the backup continues on the next
carrier.
.PP
A fileset is a named set of paths to protect, with exclusions.
A backup is a named backup of one fileset, with one or more carriers, used one
after the other.
Every write adds one tarball to a carrier, with a delete list: a Python
script in
.I tmp/
of the tarball that removes the paths deleted since they were written.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI add\-fileset " fileset path" ...
Add a fileset and scan it.
A path that starts with
.B ^
is an exclusion.
.TP
.BI add\-paths " fileset path" ...
Add paths and exclusions to a fileset and scan it.
.TP
.BI update\-filesets " fileset" ...
Scan filesets again, for new, changed and removed files.
Run it before every write.
.TP
.BI add\-backup " backup fileset"
Add a backup of a fileset.
.TP
.BI rename\-backup " old new"
Rename a backup.
.TP
.BI add\-carrier " backup label" ...
Add carriers to a backup.
A write goes to the first carrier that is not full, by label in alphabetical
order.
.TP
.BI write " backup mountpoint"
Write a tarball of the backup to a mounted drive, as
.IR mountpoint /backup\- N .tar.
.TP
.BI write\-tape " backup device"
Write a tarball of the backup to a tape drive, through
.BR mbuffer (1)
and
.BR blockwrite (1),
on the non-rewinding device, like
.IR /dev/nst0 .
The tape must be rewound; it is rewound again at the end.
.TP
.BR summary " [\fIbackup\fR...]"
Show the state of the backups; the names can hold
.B *
as a wildcard.
.TP
.B list\-filesets
.TQ
.B list\-backups
.TQ
.B list\-carrier
.TQ
.B list\-tarballs
List the filesets, backups, carriers or tarballs.
.TP
.BI manifest " label"
List the tarballs on a carrier and every file and symlink in them.
.TP
.BI remove\-carrier " label" ...
.TQ
.BI remove\-backups " backup" ...
Remove carriers or backups, with what belongs to them, from the database.
The files on the carriers are left alone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when a command fails, or reports an error and goes on with
the rest of its work; 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hyprdebian/hd\-backup.db
The database, one per user.
A command run with
.B sudo
uses the one of root.
It is the only record of what is on which carrier: keep a copy of it
elsewhere.
.SH NOTES
Writing to tape needs
.BR mt\-st (1)
and
.BR mbuffer (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blockwrite (1),
.BR hd\-backup\-prep (8),
.BR hd\-backup\-load (8),
.BR hd\-backup\-vm (8),
.BR tar (1)
